    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor lineup, anchored by **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.09). **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits immensely from the park factor against Suarez, whose 3.91 xERA is the most exploitable pitching matchup among our top-tier plays. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable platoon split against Lynch IV to maintain an elite outlook. **Kyle Tucker** (72.94) remains a must-start despite an assumed #7 spot in the order, as the 5.48 xERA of Jackson Kent provides the softest landing spot of the day, effectively neutralizing the positional penalty. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.12) and **Coby Mayo** (66.25) round out the core, with **Coby Mayo** enjoying a +16% park adjustment that helps him bridge the gap against a competent arm in Suarez.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Henry Bolte**, who finished with a 43.24 score. While his elite speed profile is always tempting for our stolen base-heavy strategy, he was squeezed out by the consistency of **Wade Meckler** and the positional utility of our depth pieces. The primary deterrent for **Henry Bolte** was the matchup against Logan Gilbert (3.52 xERA), whose ability to suppress quality contact significantly depressed **Henry Bolte**'s base projection, ultimately leaving him on the outside looking in. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several slots\u2014specifically **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014are currently pending official lineup confirmation. While we have modeled them into these optimal spots, managers should monitor for late scratches. Additionally, **Gunnar Henderson** faces a -15% drag due to his platoon split against Suarez; while his talent keeps him in the 60+ \"Strong\" range, he remains a high-variance play relative to the safer profiles of **Luis Robert Jr.** or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**. We continue to carry **Andy Pages** on the IL, as he remains unavailable for selection.",
